  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A point charge <math><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> is placed just outside an imaginary hemispherical surface of radius R as shown in the figure. Which of the following statements is/are correct?<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/kvnyxksmvpgjywwrtbbzeqteagykaipvweotnmcenckdanzuir.jpeg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "md82L",
      "text": "The circumference of the flat surface is an equipotential",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xPmFQ",
      "text": "The electric flux passing through the curved surface of the hemisphere is <math><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>&epsilon;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JgEAS",
      "text": "Total flux through the curved and the flat surfaces is  <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DaW1i",
      "text": "The component of the electric field normal to the flat surface is constant over the surface",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Every point on circumference of flat surface is at equal distance from point charge </p><p>Hence circumference is equipotential.</p><p>Flux passing through curved surface = - flux passing through flat surface.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/13_solu_phy_pa_2.jpg\"/></p><p><math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo><mi> </mi><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow><mo>∈</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mo>.</mo><mi> </mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></math></p><p><math><mo>∴</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">∫</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow><mo>∈</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi> </mi><mrow><munderover><mo stretchy=\"false\">∫</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mo>∈</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math><mo>∴</mo></math>     Flux through curved surface <math><mo>=</mo><mi> </mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mo>∈</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Note: Flux through surface can be calculated using concept of solid angle.</p><p><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/13_solu_phy_pa_2_1.jpg\"/></p><p><math><mo>∴</mo></math>    Solid angle subtended<math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math><mi>ϕ</mi></math> for  <math><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></math> solid angle <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>∈</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math><mo>∴</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi>ϕ</mi></math> for  <math><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> solid angle <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow><mo>∈</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mo>.</mo><mi> </mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mo>∈</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
